    "durationMs": 354749,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully tested. Here's what I built in /workspace:\n\n**Implementation**\n- Rails 8 API-only app (`rails new . --api --database=postgresql`) with a `Link` model (`code`, `url` as `text`, `clicks` default 0) and a unique index on `code`\n- `LinksController` with `POST /links` (custom or auto-generated 8-char base58 codes), `GET /links` (ascending by id, `{\"items\": [...], \"total\": n}`), `GET /links/:code`, and `GET /r/:code` (atomic `increment_counter` + 302 with `allow_other_host`)\n- Error mapping: malformed JSON, bad/missing URL, bad code → 422 with `error`; duplicate custom code → 409; unknown code → 404\n- DB config is entirely `DATABASE_URL`-driven; `start.sh` pins the environment, runs `db:prepare`, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; README documents startup\n\n**Two environment issues I found and fixed**\n1. The bundled `json` 3.1.0 gem removed the `quirks_mode` option that ActiveSupport still passes, making every `render json:` a 500 — pinned `json ~> 2.9.1`\n2. Rails escapes `&` as `\\u0026` in JSON — disabled via `escape_html_entities_in_json = false` so returned URLs are byte-identical to the input; also cleared `config.hosts` so the API answers under any hostname/IP\n\n**Validation**: a 38-check HTTP suite passes (creation, generated codes, duplicates, all 4xx paths, exact click counting, ordering), long URLs round-trip, and data plus click counts survived two cold restarts via `sh start.sh`. The test server is stopped, leaving port 8000 free."
  }
